@neilpang's suggestion is correct -- pinning a version tag does stop it. Only the `latest`/master image is built with `AUTO_UPGRADE=1`; version-tagged images (e.g. `3.0.9`) are built with it unset, so the `--cron` auto-upgrade (`if [ "$AUTO_UPGRADE" = "1" ]`) never fires and the script won't download `master.tar.gz`.

One catch for your case: running `latest` persists `AUTO_UPGRADE='1'` into your mounted `account.conf` on each auto-upgrade, and `--cron` sources that file on startup -- so it can re-enable itself even under a pinned image. Remove (or set to `0`) the `AUTO_UPGRADE` line in `/home/xxx/.acme.sh/account.conf`, then run the pinned tag.

Then updates come from pulling a new image (Watchtower or `docker pull`), which is the model you want.

